{
  "case_id": "2009-08-1198",
  "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1198",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96a930e090c5-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:02 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Seth P. Waxman, on behalf of the Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1198",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96a930e090c5-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Unlike courts, arbitrators derive their authority solely from the consent of the parties to a particular agreement."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1198",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96a930e090c5-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Waxman, there\u2019s a preliminary question in this case, and that is: There was one agreement, undoubtedly signed by both sides, and that was the one to submit to the arbitrator the question whether the arbitration clause permitted class treatment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Seth P. Waxman, on behalf of the Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1198",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96a930e090c5-0000-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is a separate statutory question that arises if the answer to the contract question is number 3. There is no meeting of the minds. It is truly silent --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1198",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96a930e090c5-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 6,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: My question was, first, the same as Justice Ginsburg."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1198",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96a930e090c5-0000-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 10,
        "start": 10
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE STEVENS: Mr. Waxman, can I ask this preliminary question? Assume the contract expressly authorized class arbitration. Would you agree that was permissible?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Seth P. Waxman, on behalf of the Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1198",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96a930e090c5-0000-0007",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "If it expressly authorized class participation, obviously, we would have no argument that the parties had not agreed to it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Seth P. Waxman, on behalf of the Petitioners",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1198",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96a930e090c5-0000-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 14,
        "start": 14
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And the AAA Rule 3, which is included on page 56 of the joint appendix, is headed \"Construction of the Arbitration Clause.\" And it requires the arbitrators in this arbitration to determine, quote, \"on construction of the arbitration clause, whether the applicable arbitration clause permits the arbitration to proceed on behalf of or against a class.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (Mr. Waxman)",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1198",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96a930e090c5-0001-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. WAXMAN: I'm sorry -- in this case, we said the contract was not truly silent, that -- essentially, we argued what Judge Rakoff concluded. They said: No, no, no; it is truly silent, but you should rule for us on other grounds."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1198",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96a930e090c5-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Mr. Waxman, may I ask you -- because your time is running and we are spending all of your time on this preliminary question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE BREYER",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1198",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96a930e090c5-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. PILLARD",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1198",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96a930e090c5-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think that if they wanted to write around it, they could do that, as this Court --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "JUSTICE STEVENS",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1198",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96a930e090c5-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 50,
        "start": 50
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "May I ask a question, a very basic, elementary questions? Where in the record is the specific question to the arbitrators found -- that they were asked to respond to?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MS. PILLARD",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1198",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96a930e090c5-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "\"Use of 'any' normally means all and includes class arbitration\" except -- \"unless expressly excluded.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Discover Bank",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1198",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96a930e090c5-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I think the case before -- Discover Bank is a party that started to put express no-class-action terms."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1198",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96a930e090c5-0003-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 59,
        "start": 59
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There are many, many contracts -- and pick up your average credit card agreement -- that will say you may not bring this as a class."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Waxman",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1198",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96a930e090c5-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "These contracts in the class are not all the same. These are form contracts that are drafted by the charterers and their brokers, and they involve different clauses, including different arbitration clauses."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "AAA",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1198",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96a930e090c5-0003-0002",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The AAA amicus brief in this case, which I commend to the Court, on behalf of no party says over and over and over again, we drafted the rules to provide procedures to answer the Bazzle contract question."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Pillard",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1198",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "96a930e090c5582bd850d08f21e22baf767083a592f7b2526ffeb317197a24ae",
      "evidence_id": "ev-96a930e090c5-0003-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 62,
        "start": 62
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the evidence was undisputed that since the days of Marco Polo the background principle in maritime law has been bilateral, rigorously bilateral."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1198",
      "confidence": 0.0,
